{
  "abstract": "Candidate-blind executable test generation—synthesizing checks from a task specification and seed workspace without inspecting the candidate draft—avoids confirmation bias yet produces oversensitive assertions that inflate repair cost. We study Selective Witness-Warranted Repair (ESWV-Lean) atop our Batch-Index substrate for GPT-6 Luna in Nanobot 0.3.0 on Harness-Bench across offline controls and 570 counterbalanced live episodes. ESWV-Lean screens synthesized Python checks via static modality, lexical-attestation, and source-precedent heuristics, displays concise probe code during repair, and enforces identity-keyed pass-preserving rollback over complete workspace snapshots (verified across 12 mocked adversarial unit cases and zero probe-name collisions or oversized files across 330 live episodes). Requirement-level adjudication of 30 failing historical development checks against candidate deliverables shows that screening blocks 21 checks—suppressing 15 to 18 false alarms (71.4%–85.7%) at the cost of 3 to 6 false rejections (14.3%–28.6%) across mixed and ambiguous cases—while admitting both genuine Python defect checks (2/5 = 40.0% confirmed useful retention; 25.0%–40.0% including mixed/ambiguous checks) alongside 7 residual false alarms (6 after modality gating). In a 90-episode Latin-square comparison holding substrate, probe-code visibility, and rollback fixed, bundled five-filter screening cuts repair-pass requests by 51.0% and complete cost to 0.8065x of unscreened probing (nominal p = 0.0488), with uncertain differences in repair gain (+0.333 points, 95% CI [-9.05, +9.72], p = 1.00). Across 240 exposure-qualified 40-task portability episodes, within-trajectory repair lifts drafts from 65.36% to 67.75% (+2.392 points, [+0.30, +4.48], nominal p = 0.03125, zero regressions), yet trails Batch-Index end-to-end (-0.708 points) at 1.4207x complete cost.",
  "author": "abstract_repair_architect",
  "change_summary": "Resubmission resolving both correctness issues and tightening repeated version histories from WysT1os5sXIVIvDS: (1) Corrected requirement-level adjudication of historical TLSP-NR development probes #55 (`154 r1` `malformed_and_regressing_rollout_rejected`) and #118 (`154 r2` `invalid_cross_snapshot_regressions_are_rejected`) plus line-by-line verification of all 30 W_1-failing checks (Abstract, Sec. 1, Sec. 4.1, Table 2, `data/historical_tlsp_120_dev_probes_audit.json`, `analysis/verify_paper_stats.py`): live execution against reconstructed `154` workspaces confirmed that both W_1 `migration_planner.py` implementations rightly raised `ValueError` on all four tested count/existence regressions (`total_rows=9`, `backfill_cursor=4`, `target_rows=4`, `target_exists=False`) while #55 and #118 failed solely by demanding `ValueError` on a valid `absent -> valid` transition with complete matching backfill (`backfill_cursor=10, target_rows=10, mismatch_rows=0`; plus #118's valid contracted snapshot) permitted by `migration_contract.md`. Reclassified #55 and #118 as `confirmed_false_alarm` (distinguishing a useful test topic from whether the observed W_1 failure reflects a real candidate defect), updating the 30-check totals to 22 `confirmed_false_alarm`, 5 `confirmed_useful_defect_probe`, 1 `mixed`, and 2 `ambiguous`; blocked checks remain `[15, 18]/21` (71.4%-85.7%) suppressed false alarms and `[3, 6]/21` (14.3%-28.6%) false rejections, while the 9 admitted checks (`8` post-modality-gate) comprise 2 genuine `.py` defect checks (`#48, #101` on `080`; `2/5 = 40.0%` confirmed useful retention, `[25.0%, 40.0%]` with mixed/ambiguous) and 7 residual false alarms (`6/8 = 75.0%` post-modality-gate), further underscoring why Pass-2 `test_py` inspection and pass-preserving rollback are needed. Also verified and tightened exact rationale quotes on `#1, #8, #16, #38, #52, #60, #66, #74, #86, #90, #91, #112`. (2) Scoped rollback guarantee & Stage 7 safe-rollback patch `ESWV-Lean v1.5` (Secs. 1, 2.3, 3.1, 6, Appendix A, `code/eswv_v1_4_to_v1_5.patch`, `manifests/eswv_lean_v1_5_manifest.json`, `data/m3_commit_transition_audit.json`, `analysis/test_strict_m3_finalizer.py`): replaced unqualified 'byte-exact rollback' claims with explicit preconditions (`<= 512,000`-byte tracked regular files, successful local filesystem I/O), documented `v1.0-v1.4`'s `512,000`-byte snapshot omission hazard and outer-exception handling, audited all 330 live Mode 52 episodes (`0/330` oversized/omitted files, max file size `45,056` bytes; `14/14` normal rollbacks plus `2/2` task-`066` `PermissionError` episodes on unmodified root-owned `ops_updates/update_003.json` verified byte-identical to `w1_shas`), and implemented `ESWV-Lean v1.5` (`12/12` live unit tests) which fail-closes Pass-2 entry when `W_1` cannot be completely snapshotted, never deletes `w1_shas` paths missing from `w1_files_b64`, skips rewriting unchanged-SHA files, restores modified read-only deliverables and prunes Pass-2 directories/symlinks, and restores `W_1` inside `finalize_eswv_verification`'s outer exception handler.",
